From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:26:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: trigger CTL_START in the encoder cleanup only
 for writeback

dpu_encoder_helper_phys_cleanup() ends with CTL_FLUSH and CTL_START for
both of its callers, the writeback and the video encoder. CTL_START
starts a writeback (or command mode) frame; the video encoder never uses
it, it has no trigger_start op and its timing engine latches the flush.

On DPU 13.0 (SM8850, Kaanapali) the CTL_START written here, after the
video timing engine is off, breaks the enable that follows in the same
commit, i.e. every modeset of a DSI video panel such as a refresh-rate
change: the new flush stays pending in CTL_FLUSH (all blocks in use:
INTF, merge 3D, DSC, the DMA pipe, both mixers), the source pipe never
fetches and the panel stays black until the display is powered off and
on again, which power-collapses the MDSS. A CTL reset at the enable does
not help.

On the OnePlus Pad 4 (DSI video panel, 144/120/60 Hz), judged by a
camera: with CTL_START skipped for video, 5 of 5 live rate changes kept
the picture; without, 0 of 3.

Only trigger CTL_START for writeback.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
index d919c6213ffc..74246be6a428 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -2344,7 +2344,15 @@ void dpu_encoder_helper_phys_cleanup(struct dpu_encoder_phys *phys_enc)
 		ctl->ops.reset_intf_cfg(ctl, &intf_cfg);
 
 	ctl->ops.trigger_flush(ctl);
-	ctl->ops.trigger_start(ctl);
+	/*
+	 * CTL_START kicks writeback here (command mode does not come here).
+	 * The video encoder never uses it: the timing engine latches the
+	 * flush. On DPU 13.x a CTL_START written once the timing engine is
+	 * off keeps the flush of an enable in the same commit (a modeset)
+	 * from latching, and the panel stays black.
+	 */
+	if (phys_enc->hw_wb)
+		ctl->ops.trigger_start(ctl);
 	ctl->ops.clear_pending_flush(ctl);
 }
 
-- 
